"p8_tags" = "macOS · Swift 6 · Open Source";
"p8_name" = "Zhen";
"p8_desc" = "Fast, native network scanner for the Mac, written entirely in Swift 6 and open-sourced across three repositories. zhen-core is the engine, the zhen command line and a privileged helper in one Swift package: it sweeps a /24 in about three seconds from unprivileged ICMP, the kernel's ARP table and Bonjour, names what it can, and says plainly what it could not work out and why. Its timing model, retransmit early and declare late, is backed by zhen-study, a pre-registered measurement study against other tooling. zhen-app is the macOS 26 SwiftUI app on top: live scans, device history and activity, notarized and collecting nothing. No subprocesses or external binaries; the core builds and tests on Linux in CI.";

"p5_tags" = "iOS · Vapor · ESP32";
"p5_name" = "Living Root";
"p5_desc" = "Full-stack hydroponic monitoring system, architected and owned end-to-end across three codebases: a SwiftUI client charting pH, EC, water temperature and level, with SwiftData snapshots so the dashboard still reads offline; a Vapor and PostgreSQL backend serving a session-authenticated admin console and a device telemetry API; and MicroPython firmware on an ESP32 sensor node reading the root zone in real time. Swift on both the app and the server, custom 3D-printed enclosures on the hardware.";

"p6_tags" = "Vapor · Leaf · JavaScript";
"p6_name" = "After Dark Stories";
"p6_desc" = "AI-assisted fiction studio, built and operated solo on a 100% Swift server: Vapor, Fluent and PostgreSQL behind server-rendered Leaf templates, with JavaScript driving the studio's editor interactions. Accounts run on database-backed sessions plus hashed access and refresh tokens, with email verification, password reset, CSRF and registration abuse protection; the admin console adds logged break-glass access and report intake. Three interface locales — English, Spanish and French — resolve from a single copy catalog. The story engine sits behind app-owned directives with output validation and a post-generation classifier. Documented brand system with design tokens, and a production posture throughout: response compression, ETag-backed static files, structured data and sitemap.";

"p7_tags" = "iOS · iPadOS · macOS";
"p7_name" = "Sideshore";
"p7_desc" = "Wind forecast and live-station app for every wind sport, in development for iPhone, iPad and Mac from one native SwiftUI target. It sets several forecast models side by side with live station readings, and gives each saved spot a GO, MARGINAL or NO verdict from fixed, readable rules covering gusts, storms and the wind's angle to that spot's shoreline, with the deciding rule shown next to the verdict. The map animates wind as particles over MapKit, with lightning, radar and storm layers. An in-house Swift package fetches everything on the device from Open-Meteo and public agencies, with request merging, rate limiting, retries and a disk cache so the app still opens offline. Alerts backtest themselves against the last 30 days.";

"p1_tags" = "iOS · iPadOS";
"p1_name" = "Tapper Counters";
"p1_desc" = "Sleek, customizable tap-to-count app for workouts, habits, scores and tallies. Per-counter colors, custom increments, sorting, and a focused full-screen counting view. SwiftUI, SwiftData and App Intents, iOS 17+.";

"p2_tags" = "macOS";
"p2_name" = "MythLog";
"p2_desc" = "Consent-first macOS app recording system events — sleep/wake, screen lock, app launches, watched-file changes, custom CLI events — into an append-only HMAC-SHA256 hash-chain ledger with a live SwiftUI timeline. Fully local, no account or analytics. macOS 14+.";

"p3_tags" = "Swift Package · Open Source";
"p3_name" = "iCalendarKit";
"p3_desc" = "Swift encoder for iCalendar data (RFC 5545) — events, alarms, timezones and recurrence rules. SPM, CI on Linux and macOS, published DocC docs. Creator and co-founder of the swift-calendar org.";

"p4_tags" = "iOS · iPadOS";
"p4_name" = "iBase";
"p4_desc" = "Fast, simple converter between binary, octal, decimal and hexadecimal. On the App Store since 2018, in English and Spanish.";

